    {
      "id": "isZ-qKxS2reaS_tz8iOeC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60.85032767705309,
      "y": 1678.7945102938177,
      "width": 890.8958333568964,
      "height": 725,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ac",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 435338576,
      "version": 1055,
      "versionNonce": 1629764432,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794205734058,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "To calculate the complexity of sorting algorithm we calculate the number of comparisons\non each pass .\n\n\nIn Bubble sort in first pass their are n-1 comaprisons on second pass n-2 comparisons\nand so on .\n\nCn = (n-1) + (n-2) + (n-3) ..............  (n-n)\n\n    =  n ( n-1 )/ 2   \n\n    =  ( n^2 - n ) / 2\n\n    =  n^2\n\nComplexity of bubble sort is quadratic .\n\n\noptimized Bubble Sort, the complexity is:\n\nCase                 Time Complexity                       Reason\n\nBest Case                O(n)                Array is already sorted only one swap is needed .\n\nAverage Case             O(n²)               Multiple comparisons and swaps are required.\n\nWorst Case               O(n²)               Array is sorted in reverse order.\n\nSpace Complexity        O(1)                Only one temporary variable is used for swapping.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "To calculate the complexity of sorting algorithm we calculate the number of comparisons on each pass .\n\n\nIn Bubble sort in first pass their are n-1 comaprisons on second pass n-2 comparisons and so on .\n\nCn = (n-1) + (n-2) + (n-3) ..............  (n-n)\n\n    =  n ( n-1 )/ 2   \n\n    =  ( n^2 - n ) / 2\n\n    =  n^2\n\nComplexity of bubble sort is quadratic .\n\n\noptimized Bubble Sort, the complexity is:\n\nCase                 Time Complexity                       Reason\n\nBest Case                O(n)                Array is already sorted only one swap is needed .            \n\nAverage Case             O(n²)               Multiple comparisons and swaps are required.\n\nWorst Case               O(n²)               Array is sorted in reverse order.\n\nSpace Complexity        O(1)                Only one temporary variable is used for swapping.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
